# Auth API

Jimu `auth-api` template: a single-tenant Go API with users, JWT authentication, RBAC, MySQL persistence and Redis sessions.

## Quick start

```bash
make up
make verify
make down
```

`make up` creates local secrets on first run, builds the stack, runs migrations and seed, and starts the API. The generated administrator password is printed once.

Set `AUTH_API_PORT` and `AUTH_API_MANAGEMENT_PORT` to change the host ports; `make verify` follows the same values.

## Stack

- API: `http://localhost:8080`
- Management: `http://localhost:9090`
- MySQL 8.4 and Redis 7 are provided by `docker-compose.yml`.
- Migrations are under `internal/migrations/mysql/`.

The project is yours to modify. `.jimu/manifest.json` records provenance and generated files only.
